{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Tehom:</b> Now he has mentioned the sea." "<b>Tehom:</b> the deep place in the sea, for when the dry land was shown, it was the gathering of the waters." "And the sense of <b>upon mountains shall waters stand</b> — this thing is known and seen in the heart, for there are waters of the sea upon high mountains, also upon walls that were built." "And the sense of <b>like a garment You covered it</b> — for the tehom is the depth of the earth and it is covered with water, for half the earth is exposed and its opposite. The words of the living Elohim — <b>upon waters shall mountains stand</b> — reversals in his heart."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {3 "The latter portion of this comment is textually difficult. 'וההופך' (lit. 'and its opposite/contrary') is taken as 'and its opposite [half is covered]'; the final phrase 'תהפוכות בלבו' ('reversals in his heart') is obscure and rendered hyper-literally; the referent of the whole clause is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:11.943343561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}